# evroc_disk (Resource)

Provides an evroc disk resource for persistent block storage.



For a lookup by name, use the [`evroc_custom_disk_image`](../data-sources/custom_disk_image.md) data source and set `image` to its `fqid`. To register an image from a bucket object, use the [`evroc_custom_disk_image`](custom_disk_image.md) resource. See [examples/custom-image-node-pool](../../examples/custom-image-node-pool) for a Kubernetes node pool booted from a baked image.

## Custom image example

Use an image already registered in the disk's project and region. Changing `image`
replaces the disk. Set `size` to at least the image's virtual disk size.

```terraform
resource "evroc_disk" "custom_boot" {
  name    = "custom-boot"
  project = "my-project"
  region  = "se-sto"
  zone    = "a"
  size    = 50
  image   = "/compute/projects/my-project/regions/se-sto/customDiskImages/node-v1"
}
```

